.TH CCOL_CIRCQ_TRY_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_circq_try_send_zc \- try to send a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_circq_try_send_zc(ccol_circular_queue *cq, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function tries to send the message immediately. If the queue is
full, it returns ccol_container_full immediately; on success it
transfers the ownership of msg->data.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq   Circular queue to send to
msg  Message to send. On success the ownership of the data moves to the
     queue.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - The function sent the message
ccol_invalid_args    - cq or msg is NULL, or the check of msg fails
ccol_not_permitted   - Sends on the queue are turned off
ccol_container_full  - The queue is full
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function never blocks.
On failure, the caller keeps the ownership of msg->data.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_circq_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_circq_timed_send_zc (3)
